        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nSuppose that we wish to find the solution to the inequality\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 2x + 6 < 12.]\n\nContent:\nAn inequality like this one can be solved just like an equation, using the addition and multiplication principles.\n\nContent:\nFirst, we apply the addition principle, subtracting [MATH: 6] from both sides:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 2x + 6|< 12; 2x + 6 \u2212 6|< 12 \u2212 6; 2x + 0|< 6; 2x|< 6]\n\nContent:\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by [MATH: 2{:}]\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 2x|< 6; (2x)/(2)|< (6)/(2); (2x)/(2)|< 3; x|< 3]\n\nContent:\nThe solution is [MATH: x < 3] In other words, any value less than [MATH: 3] satisfies the inequality.\n\nContent:\nLet's see another example."
      },
