        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Solve the inequality <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10x - 4 &gt; 16.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Solve the inequality [MATH: 10x - 4 > 16.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we apply the addition principle, adding <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 4]</span> to both sides:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10x \u2212 4|&gt; 16; 10x \u2212 4 + 4|&gt; 16 + 4; 10x + 0|&gt; 20; 10x|&gt; 20]</span></p><p>Second, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10{:}]</span></p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 10x|&gt; 20; (10x)/(10)|&gt; (20)/(10); (10x)/(10)|&gt; 2; x|&gt; 2]</span></p><p>Therefore, the solution is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x&gt; 2.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we apply the addition principle, adding [MATH: 4] to both sides:\n\n[MATH: 10x \u2212 4|> 16; 10x \u2212 4 + 4|> 16 + 4; 10x + 0|> 20; 10x|> 20]\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by [MATH: 10{:}]\n\n[MATH: 10x|> 20; (10x)/(10)|> (20)/(10); (10x)/(10)|> 2; x|> 2]\n\nTherefore, the solution is [MATH: x> 2.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nSolve the inequality [MATH: 10x - 4 > 16.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we apply the addition principle, adding [MATH: 4] to both sides:\n\n[MATH: 10x \u2212 4|> 16; 10x \u2212 4 + 4|> 16 + 4; 10x + 0|> 20; 10x|> 20]\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by [MATH: 10{:}]\n\n[MATH: 10x|> 20; (10x)/(10)|> (20)/(10); (10x)/(10)|> 2; x|> 2]\n\nTherefore, the solution is [MATH: x> 2.]"
      },
