          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Solve the inequality <span class=\"math\">[MATH: -2x + 3  &gt; -1.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Solve the inequality [MATH: -2x + 3 > -1.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 3]</span> from both sides:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u2212 2x + 3|&gt; \u2212 1; \u2212 2x + 3 \u2212 3|&gt; \u2212 1 \u2212 3; \u2212 2x + 0|&gt; \u2212 4; \u2212 2x|&gt; \u2212 4]</span></p><p>Then, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: -2.]</span> </p><p>Remember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u2212 2x|&gt; \u2212 4; (\u2212 2x)/(\u2212 2)|&lt;(\u2212 4)/(\u2212 2); (\u2212 2x)/(\u2212 2)|&lt;2; x|&lt;2]</span></p><p>Therefore, the solution is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x&lt;2.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting [MATH: 3] from both sides:\n[MATH: \u2212 2x + 3|> \u2212 1; \u2212 2x + 3 \u2212 3|> \u2212 1 \u2212 3; \u2212 2x + 0|> \u2212 4; \u2212 2x|> \u2212 4]\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by [MATH: -2.]\n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n[MATH: \u2212 2x|> \u2212 4; (\u2212 2x)/(\u2212 2)|<(\u2212 4)/(\u2212 2); (\u2212 2x)/(\u2212 2)|<2; x|<2]\n\nTherefore, the solution is [MATH: x<2.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nSolve the inequality [MATH: -2x + 3 > -1.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we apply the addition principle, subtracting [MATH: 3] from both sides:\n[MATH: \u2212 2x + 3|> \u2212 1; \u2212 2x + 3 \u2212 3|> \u2212 1 \u2212 3; \u2212 2x + 0|> \u2212 4; \u2212 2x|> \u2212 4]\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by [MATH: -2.]\n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n[MATH: \u2212 2x|> \u2212 4; (\u2212 2x)/(\u2212 2)|<(\u2212 4)/(\u2212 2); (\u2212 2x)/(\u2212 2)|<2; x|<2]\n\nTherefore, the solution is [MATH: x<2.]"
