          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 5]</span> from both sides:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u2212 11|\u2264 \u2212 8y + 5; \u2212 11 \u2212 5|\u2264 \u2212 8y + 5 \u2212 5; \u2212 16|\u2264 \u2212 8y + 0; \u2212 16|\u2264 \u2212 8y]</span></p><p>Then, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: -8.]</span> </p><p>Remember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \u2212 16|\u2264\u2212 8y; (\u2212 16)/(\u2212 8)|\u2265(\u2212 8y)/(\u2212 8); 2|\u2265(\u2212 8y)/(\u2212 8); 2|\u2265y]</span></p><p>Finally, let&#x27;s swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side. Remember, we also need to flip the inequality.</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: y \\le   2]</span></p><p>Therefore, the solution is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: y \\le   2.]</span> </p>",
            "readable_text": "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting [MATH: 5] from both sides:\n\n[MATH: \u2212 11|\u2264 \u2212 8y + 5; \u2212 11 \u2212 5|\u2264 \u2212 8y + 5 \u2212 5; \u2212 16|\u2264 \u2212 8y + 0; \u2212 16|\u2264 \u2212 8y]\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by [MATH: -8.]\n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n[MATH: \u2212 16|\u2264\u2212 8y; (\u2212 16)/(\u2212 8)|\u2265(\u2212 8y)/(\u2212 8); 2|\u2265(\u2212 8y)/(\u2212 8); 2|\u2265y]\n\nFinally, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side. Remember, we also need to flip the inequality.\n\n[MATH: y \\le 2]\n\nTherefore, the solution is [MATH: y \\le 2.]",
